// us.irs.rev_proc_87_57 — IRS Rev. Proc. 87-57: depreciation tables of
// 26 U.S.C. §168 (1987-2 C.B. 687–), the differential oracle.
//
// WHY A PACKAGE. The Year1/asset-class rules of §168 compute allowances by
// statutory arithmetic (`us.irc.deductions::168-acrs.law`: the module comment
// records agreement with 87-57 Tables 1/2 as corroboration, not source).
// Testers need the printed percent tables as an independent oracle to
// differentially check that arithmetic — pinned here, never as rule input.
// One table (Table 1: GDS 200/150% DB, half-year) is machine-readable this
// wave; the rest are inventoried with page anchors for later waves.
//
// WHAT IT HOLDS (phase 1, still rule-less). `sources/rp-87-57/en.txt` —
// the pinned `pdftotext -layout` extraction of 1987-2 C.B. 687–
// (PINNED_UNOFFICIAL_COPY; the granule PDF bytes live in
// `docs/foundations/us-irc/raw/cb1987/`, PINNED_OFFICIAL_BYTES).
// `sources.law` — source/edition/publication + SEC.1 purpose fragment +
// Table 1 fragment. `sources/tables/rp8757-table-01.lawtable.json` —
// Table 1 as structure (year × recovery class → percent as printed,
// column sums validated to 100). Everything derived is GENERATED by
// `corpus/tools/sources/sync/sync_us_irs_rev_proc_87_56_87_57.py`, never
// hand-edited. No rules: percents never enter deduction rules.
//
// LAYOUT NOTE. `check_laws_tree` §3.5 derives `us/rev-proc-87-57` from
// jurisdiction US + instrument guidance (`us.irs` is not a GROUP_BY_NAME_PREFIX
// group): the package name keeps the `irs` issuer segment, the path does not.
//
// OUT OF SCOPE. All other SEC.8 tables (mid-quarter Q2, mid-month, ADS —
// inventoried in provenance, not parsed); the 87-56 class table (sibling
// package `us.irs.rev_proc_87_56`).

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irs.rev_proc_87_57 version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irs:rev_proc_87_57:clir";
